!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Before and after selection procedures, plasmid DNA was extracted using enzymatic yeast cell wall degradation in combination with standard extraction methods. The gRNA barcodes amplified from the one-copy-per-cell CEN-plasmids. Illumina sequencing was performed in paired-end and 75-100 base pairs read length on NextSeq500 machines with 15% PhiX spike-in.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = DNA barcode libraries were generated by introducing standard Illumina P5 and P7 adapters and inline sample barcodes by PCR. Library preparation is otherwise performed according to standard Illumina protocols
!Sample_description = PCR-amplified DNA barcodes
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: CRISPR screen
!Sample_data_processing = Sequencing data was demultiplexed with Jemultiplexer with standard parameters and base call quality controlled with FastQC. Reads were trimmed and aligned to the FASTA of DNA barcode sequences (FASTA available on series record) with the Burrows-Wheeler algorithm to compute read counts.
!Sample_data_processing = Fold changes for gRNA barcodes and for genes were computed in R code using the edgeR package, although other read-count based packages can be used alternatively, such as limma or DeSeq2. Read counts were normalized by library size. Fitness fold changes were calculated as contrasts between +ATc and -ATc condition (+ATc/-ATc) of populations that underwent competitive growth selection in any of the used media. Gene log2FCs were computed as mean log2FC of all gRNAs per gene. Alternatively, these can be computed without prior calculation of gRNA log2FCs by starting the edgeR analysis from the geometric mean of readcounts per gene. We further calculate rank-based gene score measures based on a subset of gRNAs with extreme effects and the median log2FC of gRNAs.
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Raw read counts and Log2 fold changes of gRNAs and genes.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL19424
!Sample_contact_name = Cosimo,,Jann
!Sample_contact_laboratory = Group of Lars M. Steinmetz
!Sample_contact_department = Genome Biology
!Sample_contact_institute = EMBL Heidelberg
!Sample_contact_address = Meyerhofstr. 1
!Sample_contact_city = Heidelberg
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = 69117
!Sample_contact_country = Germany
!Sample_instrument_model = NextSeq 500
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic
!Sample_library_strategy = OTHER
